My standard AK:

Amulets: Life Saving (as many as possible), Magical Breating (switch to
for certain situations)

Armor: exactly the same as your list, only GoD instead of GoP (better
spells), and a (greased) helm of brilliance instead of Dwarvish (ditto).
Depends a lot on whether you want spells or combat power.

Weapons: Grayswandir, *Brand, MagicBane, or Mojo depending on class.  I
don't #twoweapon, but if you do, a silver saber is a good second weapon.

Food: a couple lizard corpses, some eucalyptus, K-rations or lembas, a tin
or two of floating eye meat (protects against accidents)

Rings: Slow Digestion, Free Action.  Switch to conflict, regen, and
levitation as needed.

Wands: 4-5 Digging (escape, Elbereth, earth), death, poly, striking
(boulders), fire/lightning (Elbereth), cold (ice), 3-4 teleport,
cancellation (sometimes)

Tools: grease, 2 blessed unicorn horns (in case one gets punked), key,
blindfold, stethoscope, oilskin sack, BoH (often put the BoH inside
Oilskin to prevent cursing), magic lamp (if possible)

Gems: luckstone

In the oilskin sack (so I can always get to them quickly): cursed ?oTele,
/oWish, holy water, b?oRC, and at least one !oFH

In the BoH: everything else... lots of holy water, full healing, blessed
?oEarth (build a fort), ?ogeno, ?ocharge, misc spellbooks, a pickaxe,
backup weapons, armor, scrolls, whatever.

You can sometimes do without some of these things... but this is what I
consider a "complete" kit.



